## What is pinned beyond the PRD's literal text

Each of these is fixed by the plan (the decision id is given) and tested as the plan states it; the reviewer may overrule any of them.

- Exact names and signatures of `itemsInRange`, `dayItemPlacement` (and its `allDay` / `timed` / `task` placement shape), `DayRange`, `DayRangeEntry`, `dayItemFromLocalEvent`, `LocalDayItem`, `agendaItemsForToday`, `decideAgendaNotice` (input `{ google, othersReady, rowCount, emptyText }`), `agendaPartialMessage`, `AGENDA_EMPTY`, `dayRouteOf`, `dayFromRoute`, the `day-view` exports (Tasks 1-6), and `ALL_DAY_LABEL` exported from `format.ts`.
- D3-1 days are the owner's days (a New York-authored Event is placed and shown on São Paulo time; an all-day date is verbatim).
- D3-3 spans: an all-day Event covers its start through the day before its exclusive end; a timed one through the day of its last instant (`end - 1`); an end that is not after the start covers the start's day (local and Google alike; a Google timed event with a mismatched end is read as ending at its start and never throws). Google rows now also appear on their later days in the Agenda, a deliberate change from the shipped start-day-only rule.
- D3-4 order: all-day, timed by start, Tasks; ties in arrival order (test/agenda.test.ts:150-159 pins it for the shipped Agenda); a continuation sorts by its real start. Split-invariance is claimed ONLY for order-preserving (contiguous) splits; an interleaved split is deliberately not tested.
- D3-8 bucketing of non-Task items: no day -> `undated`, after today -> `upcoming`, otherwise `today` (so a past-dated Event lands in `today`, the plan's accepted cost). The PRD clause (never `overdue`/`done`/`missed`) and this placement are kept in separate describes.
- D3-10 copy: the continuation label `até HH:mm` (flagged in the plan for the owner), `HH:mm–HH:mm` with U+2013 and no spaces, an end at midnight reading `00:00`, `Nada neste dia.`, the heading `terça-feira, 20 de outubro` (year added only when it differs from today's), the literal paths `/api/events?from=..&to=..` and `/api/google/events[?from=..&to=..]`.
- Deliberately NOT pinned (the plan is silent): the `endMs` of a reversed or mismatched-end timed item; the label on a middle day of a timed item spanning three or more days; `agendaPartialMessage(0)`; `pathOf` of a day route holding an invalid date; the order of `splitDayItems`' keys; error wording.

